 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation (Lascierò, straziar mi il crine, in contento, and Masétto with the print's accent in bar 47, where the libretto has Lascerò, straziarmi, In contenti/contento and Masetto). IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S26) and the IPA was checked against Castel. Zerlina sings the first four lines twice before the next four, with repeats of starò qui and saprò baciar; the Allegro repeats Pace, pace and notte e dì vogliam passar, with sì and vogliam added. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
